# BLoC Authoring Rules

All business logic is implemented as `@RxBloc()` classes generated via **`rx_bloc_generator`** and composed with **`rxdart`**. These conventions are enforced by every existing BLoC in the codebase and MUST be followed for new ones.

## 1. File Layout

- One bloc per file: `<name>_bloc.dart` next to any sibling in `blocs/` folder.
- Generated code goes into `<name>_bloc.rxb.g.dart` and is pulled in via `part`.
- Optional companion part files (all siblings in `blocs/`, all declared `part of '<name>_bloc.dart';`):
  - `<name>_bloc_extensions.dart` — complex private helpers: multi-field validation, DTO mapping, reusable stream-composition extensions. See §10.
  - `<name>_bloc_models.dart` — bloc-private models, enums, and sealed signal types (e.g. `_GithubSearchFailureScope`, `_GithubSearchFetchRequest`).
    - **Create this file when the bloc declares two or more such types, OR a single type that carries real state (one or more fields / enum values with payloads).**
    - **Do NOT create this file** for a single empty marker class or a single enum with no data — inline those at the bottom of `<name>_bloc.dart` to avoid churn.
- Always declare the `part` directives **before** the contract classes.

```dart
part 'login_bloc.rxb.g.dart';
part 'login_bloc_extensions.dart'; // optional, only if it exists
part 'login_bloc_models.dart';     // optional, only if it exists
```

## 2. Three-Class Skeleton

Every bloc exposes exactly three top-level declarations in this order:

1. `abstract class <Name>BlocEvents` — one `void` method per user-initiated action.
2. `abstract class <Name>BlocStates` — one getter per observable state, typed as `Stream<T>` or `ConnectableStream<T>`.
3. `@RxBloc() class <Name>Bloc extends $<Name>Bloc` — the implementation.

Doc-comment each event/state. The `$<Name>Bloc` base class is generated — never write it by hand.

```dart
abstract class DashboardBlocEvents {
  void fetchData();
}

abstract class DashboardBlocStates {
  Stream<bool> get isLoading;
  Stream<ErrorModel> get errors;
  Stream<Result<String>> get data;
}

@RxBloc()
class DashboardBloc extends $DashboardBloc {
  DashboardBloc(this._service);

  final DashboardService _service;

  @override
  Stream<Result<String>> _mapToDataState() => _$fetchDataEvent
      .startWith(null)
      .switchMap((_) => _service.fetchData().asResultStream())
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .shareReplay(maxSize: 1);

  @override
  Stream<bool> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingState;

  @override
  Stream<ErrorModel> _mapToErrorsState() => errorState.mapToErrorModel();
}
```

## 3. Events

- Fire-and-forget methods returning `void`. Parameters are the payload.
- Use `@RxBlocEvent(type: RxBlocEventType.behaviour, seed: <value>)` for inputs that must replay their latest value (text fields, filters, pagination reset flags). Default (`publish`) is fine for one-shot actions like `login()` or `loadPage()`.
- Inside the bloc, subscribe to the generated `_$<eventName>Event` stream; never invoke the public method from within the class except to trigger a self-dispatch.

```dart
@RxBlocEvent(type: RxBlocEventType.behaviour, seed: '')
void setEmail(String email);

void login();
```

## 4. States

- Standard triplet present on nearly every bloc: `Stream<bool> isLoading`, `Stream<ErrorModel> errors`, plus feature-specific streams.
- Wire `isLoading`/`errors` via the generated handlers — do not reinvent them:

```dart
@override
Stream<bool> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingState;

@override
Stream<ErrorModel> _mapToErrorsState() => errorState.mapToErrorModel();
```

- If different async actions need distinct loading scopes, switch the state to `Stream<LoadingWithTag>` and return `loadingWithTagState`; tag each `asResultStream(tag: ...)`:

```dart
abstract class CounterBlocStates {
  Stream<LoadingWithTag> get isLoading;
  // ...
}

@RxBloc()
class CounterBloc extends $CounterBloc {
  static const tagIncrement = 'Increment';
  static const tagDecrement = 'Decrement';

  @override
  Stream<LoadingWithTag> _mapToIsLoadingState() => loadingWithTagState;

  @override
  Stream<int> _mapToCountState() => Rx.merge<Result<Count>>([
        _$incrementEvent.switchMap(
          (_) => _service.increment().asResultStream(tag: tagIncrement),
        ),
        _$decrementEvent.switchMap(
          (_) => _service.decrement().asResultStream(tag: tagDecrement),
        ),
      ])
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .whereSuccess()
      .map((e) => e.value)
      .shareReplay(maxSize: 1);
}
```

- Use `@RxBlocIgnoreState()` on getters that only proxy an event stream or a `BehaviorSubject`; do not implement them via `_mapTo...State`.
- State streams that must survive rebuilds end with `.shareReplay(maxSize: 1)`. Use `ConnectableStream<T>` + `.publish()` / `.publishReplay(maxSize: 1)` when the stream must be active **before** any UI subscribes (routing, login success, one-shot effects). Call `xxx.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription)` from the constructor.

```dart
@RxBloc()
class LoginBloc extends $LoginBloc {
  LoginBloc(this._service, this._router) {
    loggedIn.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription);
    onRouting.connect().addTo(_compositeSubscription);
  }

  @override
  ConnectableStream<bool> _mapToLoggedInState() => _$loginEvent
      .exhaustMap((_) => _service.login().asResultStream())
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .whereSuccess()
      .doOnData((_) => _router.go(const DashboardRoute().routeLocation))
      .startWith(false)
      .publish();
}
```

## 5. Dependency Injection

- Inject **services** (not repositories, not data sources) via the constructor; keep fields `final` and private.
- For cross-bloc signalling, inject a shared coordinator type (e.g. `CoordinatorBlocType`) instead of another feature bloc.
- For navigation, inject `GoRouter` and route via typed routes: `_router.go(const DashboardRoute().routeLocation)`.

## 6. Stream Composition Guide

| Situation | Operator |
|---|---|
| New input supersedes the in-flight request | `switchMap` |
| Ignore taps while a request is in flight (login, register) | `exhaustMap` / `throttleTime(...)` |
| Combine latest values of multiple streams on an event | `withLatestFrom` / `withLatestFromN` |
| Merge heterogeneous triggers into one pipeline | `Rx.merge([...])` with a small private sealed signal type |
| Text search debouncing | `.debounceTime(...)` + `.distinct()` before the network call |

Always finish an async pipeline with `.asResultStream()` → `.setResultStateHandler(this)`; use `.whereSuccess()` / `.whereError()` afterwards. This is what plugs the pipeline into `loadingState` and `errorState` automatically.

### 6.1 Inline compositions over throwaway locals

Prefer composing streams **inline** inside `Rx.merge([...])`, `switchMap(...)`, `withLatestFrom(...)`, etc. Do **not** pull a one-shot composition into a `final queryRequests = ...` style local just to reference it once on the next line — it adds a naming step without improving clarity and hides the pipeline shape.

```dart
// PREFERRED: the shape of the pipeline is visible at a glance.
return Rx.merge<_FetchRequest>([
  _$setSearchQueryEvent
      .map((q) => q.trim())
      .debounceTime(const Duration(milliseconds: 350))
      .distinct()
      .map(_QueryRequest.new),
  Rx.merge<bool>([
    _$loadPageEvent,
    _$retryLastFetchEvent.map((_) => _lastFailureScope != _FailureScope.append),
  ]).throttleTime(kBackpressureDuration).map(_PageRequest.new),
]).switchMap(_handleRequest).setResultStateHandler(this); // ...
```

```dart
// AVOID: temporary locals used only once downstream.
final queryRequests = _$setSearchQueryEvent
    .map((q) => q.trim())
    .debounceTime(const Duration(milliseconds: 350))
    .distinct()
    .map(_QueryRequest.new);

final pageRequests = Rx.merge<bool>([
  _$loadPageEvent,
  _$retryLastFetchEvent.map((_) => _lastFailureScope != _FailureScope.append),
]).throttleTime(kBackpressureDuration).map(_PageRequest.new);

return Rx.merge([queryRequests, pageRequests]).switchMap(_handleRequest)...;
```

Only extract a local when the **same** composition is consumed by two or more downstream operators (e.g. a `publish()`ed stream used both to drive a request and to refresh a UI signal) — and in that case, consider lifting it to a named method or extension (§10) instead.

## 7. Internal State via Subjects

Whenever a bloc needs to remember a value between events (last query, current failure scope, flag, counter, model, …), back it with a **stream-shaped container** rather than a plain field.

- Use `BehaviorSubject<T>.seeded(initial)` for single latest values, `ReplaySubject<T>` for short histories, `PublishSubject<T>` for one-shot notifications. Default to `BehaviorSubject` for state.
- Mutate via `.add(...)`, read the current value via `.value` (for `BehaviorSubject`) only when strictly necessary — prefer composing the subject with `rxdart` operators (`withLatestFrom`, `switchMap`, `distinctUnique`, `scan`, …) from inside `_mapTo...State` pipelines.
- Expose the subject externally only through a `Stream<T>` getter, typically wired with `@RxBlocIgnoreState()`; never leak the `BehaviorSubject` itself through the state contract.
- **Every subject the bloc owns MUST be `.close()`d in `dispose()` before `super.dispose()`**.

```dart
final _lastEvaluatedQuerySubject = BehaviorSubject<String>.seeded('');
final _lastFailureScopeSubject =
    BehaviorSubject<_FailureScope>.seeded(_FailureScope.refresh);

@override
@RxBlocIgnoreState()
Stream<String> get lastEvaluatedQuery =>
    _lastEvaluatedQuerySubject.distinct();

@override
Stream<bool> _mapToCanRetryState() => _lastFailureScopeSubject
    .map((scope) => scope != _FailureScope.none)
    .distinct()
    .shareReplay(maxSize: 1);

@override
void dispose() {
  _lastEvaluatedQuerySubject.close();
  _lastFailureScopeSubject.close();
  super.dispose();
}
```

Plain fields (`String _foo = ''`, `bool _isDirty = false`, `_FailureScope _lastFailureScope = ...`) are an anti-pattern for bloc state: downstream pipelines cannot react to them, tests cannot observe their transitions, and disposal semantics get fuzzy. Convert them to `BehaviorSubject`s.

## 8. Subscriptions & Disposal

- Every subscription / `connect()` MUST be piped through `.addTo(_compositeSubscription)` — the base class disposes it.
- Every `BehaviorSubject` / `ReplaySubject` / `PublishSubject` the bloc owns MUST be `.close()`d in an overridden `dispose()`; call `super.dispose()` last.

```dart
final _paginatedListSubject =
    BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<Item>>.seeded(
      PaginatedList(list: [], pageSize: _pageSize),
    );

@override
void dispose() {
  _paginatedListSubject.close();
  super.dispose();
}
```

## 9. Pagination (`rx_bloc_list`)

When a state is a `Stream<PaginatedList<T>>`:

- Back it with `final _paginated = BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<T>>.seeded(PaginatedList(list: [], pageSize: _pageSize));`.
- Expose `void loadPage({bool reset = false})` (or equivalent) as the sole event; on `reset: true` call `_paginated.value.reset()` before fetching.
- Use `pageToLoad` (or `pageNumber + 1`) as the page argument, `.switchMap` into the service, then `.setResultStateHandler(this).mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated).bind(_paginated)` and return `_paginated` from `_mapTo...State`.

```dart
@override
Stream<PaginatedList<Item>> _mapToItemsState() => _$loadPageEvent
    .startWith(false)
    .switchMap((reset) {
      if (reset) _paginated.value.reset();
      return _service
          .getItems(
            page: _paginated.value.pageNumber + 1,
            pageSize: _pageSize,
          )
          .asResultStream();
    })
    .setResultStateHandler(this)
    .mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated)
    .bind(_paginated);
```

For **debounced-search + pagination in one pipeline**, `Rx.merge` the two triggers into a private sealed signal type (living in `<name>_bloc_models.dart`, §1), `switchMap` once, and reset the paginated list when a query arrives. Compose the two trigger streams **inline** (§6.1) — do not extract them into throwaway locals:

```dart
// In products_bloc_models.dart
part of 'products_bloc.dart';

/// Discriminated union describing what triggered the next fetch.
sealed class _FetchTrigger {}

final class _FilterTrigger extends _FetchTrigger {
  _FilterTrigger(this.filter);
  final String filter;
}

final class _PageTrigger extends _FetchTrigger {
  _PageTrigger({required this.reset});
  final bool reset;
}
```

```dart
// In products_bloc.dart
ProductsBloc(this._service) {
  Rx.merge<_FetchTrigger>([
    _$onFilterChangedEvent
        .map((v) => v.trim())
        .debounceTime(const Duration(milliseconds: 300))
        .distinct()
        .map(_FilterTrigger.new),
    _$loadPageEvent.map((reset) => _PageTrigger(reset: reset)),
  ])
      .switchMap((trigger) {
        // A new filter (or explicit refresh) always restarts pagination.
        if (trigger is _FilterTrigger || (trigger as _PageTrigger).reset) {
          _paginated.value.reset();
        }
        if (trigger is _FilterTrigger) {
          _currentFilterSubject.add(trigger.filter);
        }

        return _service
            .fetchProducts(
              filter: _currentFilterSubject.value,
              page: _paginated.value.pageNumber + 1,
              pageSize: _pageSize,
            )
            .asResultStream();
      })
      .setResultStateHandler(this)
      .mergeWithPaginatedList(_paginated)
      .bind(_paginated)
      .addTo(_compositeSubscription);
}
```

## 10. Extensions & Complex Logic Decomposition

When a `_mapTo...State` body grows past a handful of operators, or when the same composition (request dispatch, scope bookkeeping, result normalization) appears in more than one place, lift it into a **self-contained extension** declared in `<name>_bloc_extensions.dart` (`part of '<name>_bloc.dart';`). This keeps `_mapTo...State` readable as a pipeline and makes each helper independently testable.

Guidelines:

- Prefer **extensions on `Stream<T>`** (or on the generated event stream types) so the helper slots into the pipeline with a single `.methodName(...)` call — preserves the linear, top-to-bottom reading order of rx pipelines.
- Extensions on a bloc type (`extension _FooBlocX on FooBloc { ... }`) are fine for non-stream helpers (scope updates, subject mutations, validation).
- Keep each extension **self-contained**: it should reference only its receiver, its parameters, and other members of the same part file — avoid reaching into unrelated bloc state.
- **Every extension and every public method on it MUST carry a doc comment** describing:
  1. **Purpose** — what the helper does and why it exists.
  2. **Parameters** — each parameter, its role, and any constraints.
  3. **Usage** — a one-line example of how it plugs into a pipeline.

```dart
// In github_search_bloc_extensions.dart
part of 'github_search_bloc.dart';

/// Stream helpers for the GitHub-search fetch pipeline.
///
/// Usage:
/// ```dart
/// Rx.merge([...]).switchMap(handler).trackFailureScope(this).setResultStateHandler(this);
/// ```
extension _GithubSearchFetchPipelineX
    on Stream<Result<PaginatedList<GithubRepositoryModel>>> {
  /// Updates the bloc's `_lastFailureScopeSubject` based on whether each
  /// emitted result represents a refresh or an append.
  ///
  /// - [bloc] — the owning bloc; its `_lastFailureScopeSubject` is mutated
  ///   as a side-effect of each emission.
  /// - [isRefresh] — callback run per emission to classify it; return `true`
  ///   for full-list refreshes, `false` for paginated appends.
  Stream<Result<PaginatedList<GithubRepositoryModel>>> trackFailureScope(
    GithubSearchBloc bloc, {
    required bool Function(Result<PaginatedList<GithubRepositoryModel>> result)
        isRefresh,
  }) =>
      doOnData((result) {
        bloc._lastFailureScopeSubject.add(
          isRefresh(result)
              ? _GithubSearchFailureScope.refresh
              : _GithubSearchFailureScope.append,
        );
      });
}
```

A good rule of thumb: if a `_mapTo...State` exceeds ~30 operator lines, or any lambda inside it spans more than ~15 lines, split the inner logic into an extension.

## 11. Things to Avoid

- Don't hand-roll `StreamController` when a generated event or `BehaviorSubject` fits.
- Don't call repositories / data sources / Dio from a bloc — always go through a service.
- Don't put UI concerns (`BuildContext`, widgets, `SnackBar`s) inside a bloc. Emit a state; let the page react via `RxBlocListener` / `RxBlocBuilder`.
- Don't mix `async`/`await` with reactive pipelines inside `_mapTo...State`; stick to `rxdart` operators so error/loading handlers wire up correctly.
- Don't emit from another bloc directly — route it through a shared coordinator bloc.
- Don't store bloc state in plain mutable fields (`String`, `bool`, `int`, model instances, enums). Back state with `BehaviorSubject<T>` and access/mutate it via rxdart operators; close the subject in `dispose()` (§7).
- Don't extract throwaway stream-composition locals (`final queryRequests = ...`) that are used exactly once downstream — inline them into the consumer (§6.1).
- Don't scatter bloc-private models / enums / sealed signals across the top of `<name>_bloc.dart` when there are two or more of them; move them to `<name>_bloc_models.dart` (§1).
- Don't let a `_mapTo...State` balloon with deeply nested lambdas — extract the inner logic into documented extensions in `<name>_bloc_extensions.dart` (§10).

## Archetype Cheatsheet

| Archetype | Shape |
|---|---|
| Minimal single-state | one event, one `_mapTo...State` using `switchMap` + `asResultStream` + `shareReplay(maxSize: 1)`. |
| Tagged loading | `Stream<LoadingWithTag>` state + multiple `Rx.merge`-ed events with `asResultStream(tag: ...)`. |
| Form + routing | `@RxBlocEvent(behaviour, seed: '')` input events, `ConnectableStream` result + routing streams connected in constructor, `withLatestFrom` to pick up current field values on submit. |
| Paginated list | `BehaviorSubject<PaginatedList<T>>` + `loadPage({bool reset = false})` + `mergeWithPaginatedList` + `bind`. |
| Debounced search + pagination | `Rx.merge` debounced query stream with page stream into a sealed signal; single `switchMap`. |
| Global event hub / coordinator | no state mapping; expose events as `@RxBlocIgnoreState()` streams so other blocs can subscribe. |
